        inf("S8.3",
            r"For a source tensor of norm at most $.5$ the source transform $\widetilde{\mathscr F}$ applies the linewise approximation of $\mathcal A$, then $\widetilde{\mathscr C}$, then the linewise approximation of $\mathcal B_0$, then multiplies the grid numerators exactly by $2^\gamma$; its exact counterpart is $2^\gamma\mathcal B_0QF_{\boldsymbol t}\mathcal A=RF_{\boldsymbol s}$, and the opposite-sign procedure is $\widetilde{\mathscr F}^+(z)=\overline{\widetilde{\mathscr F}(\overline z)}$ with counterpart $RF_{\boldsymbol s}^+$.",
            r"computed chirp transform $\widetilde{\mathscr C}$, apply the linewise"),
        inf("S8.4",
            r"Input conversion: read each operand backward in groups of $b$ bits to obtain the radix-$2^b$ digits $a_0,\dots,a_{q-1}$, write digit $a_j$ as the exact grid numerator $a_j2^{p-b-2}$ in a signed $w_{\rm c}$-bit real word with a zero imaginary word (value $a_j2^{-b-2}$), and append $S-q$ zero records, in time $O(n+Sp)=O(Tp)$.",
            r"$a_j2^{p-b-2}$ in a signed $w_{\rm c}$-bit real word, followed by a zero"),
        inf("S8.5",
            r"Steps 1-2: apply the coefficient-address map $\Phi$ with its padded layout to obtain source arrays $u,v$ of exact grid values of norm below $1/4$, then compute $\widetilde{\mathscr F}(u)$ and $\widetilde{\mathscr F}(v)$.",
            r"\item Apply the coefficient-address map $\Phi$, with its padded layout, to obtain"),
